5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,I want to know which past projects actually worked for the people using them. Who else cares about real user satisfaction?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"I’m concerned about how timetable disruptions and post-completion usage rates are overlooked. We need data on operational impact, not just satisfaction.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’m curious about the delivery schedules. Why do projects always stretch beyond their initial timelines?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I’m worried the approved costs don’t match reality. Who else thinks we need to check if the budget figures actually hold up?,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"I’m tired of the same few people absorbing every extra task. Who else is tracking the staffing strain behind these ""improvements""?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, operational impact is vital, but without knowing if users are actually happy, we might just be optimizing for empty rooms.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, satisfaction is subjective. I need objective metrics on how long rooms are out of service and how they are booked afterward.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, objective metrics are lovely, but they rarely capture the chaos of a schedule that keeps slipping. I’d rather see the actual delivery delays.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, delays are real, but I worry the final price tag is the real shock. We need to see if the paper numbers survive the market.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, cost overruns are predictable. The real crisis is that the same exhausted staff keep absorbing the fallout. We need to see the staffing posts.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, exhaustion is real, but if the facility itself is flawed, no amount of staffing fixes the core problem. We must verify actual user experience.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, flawed facilities cause the disruptions. I need to see the timetable records to quantify exactly how much service is lost during construction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, quantifying lost service is sensible, but it ignores the root cause: the calendar itself is a fiction. I need to see the decade of delivery schedules.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree the calendar is fiction, but I need to know if the money vanishes too. I’ll check the tender records and renewal reserves.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, checking the money is fine, but it ignores the human cost. I’ll look into staffing posts and bench technicians' routines to prove the strain.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, I accept your need for objective data. I will examine the post-occupancy review ratings and survey findings in the older blocks to verify actual user satisfaction.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Victoria,,I will examine the timetable records on rooms out of service and the booking data for specialist and general rooms.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll examine the decade of delivery schedules by project rationale and the weather days in the site diaries.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Kenji,,I’ll examine the tender records over three budget cycles and the renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,I’ll examine the staffing posts since the hiring freeze and the bench technicians' weekly manual routines.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
