35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, the data confirms my suspicion. Projects succeed only when shared. Single-wing benefits fail. We must prioritize open, multi-department spaces.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, my data shows specialist rooms sit idle while general rooms are overbooked. We are wasting capital on low-usage spaces.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, your idle rooms are a symptom, not the cause. My data shows comfort-driven projects slip a year. We must prioritize inspection-driven work to keep the calendar honest.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, delays are bad, but my data shows plant costs jumped twenty percent. We need to budget for real market rates, not old paper figures.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, twenty percent is a number. My data shows technicians logging hours on manual checks because equipment fails. We’re paying for labor to fix design flaws.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, your point is valid, but if the space is inherently flawed, no amount of manual labor fixes it. We must design for shared success, not just patch leaks.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, your labor costs are real, but my data proves the space itself is misallocated. We must stop building idle specialist rooms and fund general capacity instead.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shunichi, manual labor is a band-aid. My data proves comfort projects slip a year. We must prioritize inspection-driven work to keep the calendar honest.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, I agree labor is a band-aid, but my data shows we never even budgeted to replace the broken gear. We’re paying twice for the same failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, paying twice is the symptom. The disease is that we never hired anyone to fix it. I’m done patching holes with exhausted bodies.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, inspection-driven work is necessary, but my data shows shared spaces succeed. We must combine your schedule discipline with multi-department access to ensure the project actually works for everyone.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, I agree on schedule discipline, but my data shows general rooms are overbooked. We must fund general capacity, not idle specialist spaces, to fix the core imbalance.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, combining is a trap. My data shows comfort projects slip a year. We must prioritize inspection-driven work to keep the calendar honest, not dilute it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree on discipline, but my data shows we ignored replacement costs. We must fund the renewal reserve now, or the market will punish us later.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, discipline is nice, but it doesn't hire people. My data shows unfilled posts and technicians doing manual work. We need to fund the staff, not just the schedule.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, I hear your caution, but shared access is the only proven success metric. We must build for everyone, not just one wing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, I agree on discipline, but my data proves general rooms are overbooked. We must fund general capacity, not idle specialist spaces, to fix the core imbalance.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, I concede the point. If the calendar is honest, we can actually deliver the general capacity you need. Let’s stop arguing and look at the candidates.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, agreed. Let’s see the candidates. I need to ensure the next plan includes a real renewal reserve, not just another paper promise.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, agreed. Let’s see the candidates. I need to ensure the next plan funds the staff, not just the schedule.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
